blocks:
  - type: metin
    baslik: The difference between anxiety and an anxiety disorder
    metin: |-
      Nervousness before an exam, excitement before an important presentation, or fear when facing a dangerous situation — these are all normal, healthy forms of anxiety. This kind of anxiety motivates and protects us.

      An anxiety disorder is different: it is a chronic state of anxiety that arises without a real threat, or with an intensity far disproportionate to any actual threat, and that negatively affects daily life, relationships, and work or academic performance.
  - type: bilgi-kutusu
    ton: yesil
    baslik: 'Awareness: How common is it?'
    metin: Approximately 284 million people worldwide live with an anxiety disorder — making anxiety the most prevalent mental health condition globally. (WHO, 2019)
  - type: kart-yigini
    baslik: Types of anxiety disorder
    kartlar:
      - baslik: Generalised Anxiety Disorder (GAD)
        metin: Excessive, uncontrollable worry across multiple areas lasting at least 6 months. Persistent concern about work, health, family, finances and similar topics.
      - baslik: Panic Disorder
        metin: Sudden, intense fear episodes ([panic attacks](/en/blog/panic-attack-symptoms.html)) characterised by palpitations, shortness of breath and fear of dying. Consists of recurring panic attacks.
      - baslik: Social Anxiety Disorder
        metin: Fear of being judged, humiliated or embarrassed in social situations. Can lead to avoidance of social interactions and isolation.
      - baslik: Specific Phobias
        metin: Disproportionate fear of specific objects or situations (heights, enclosed spaces, flying, spiders, etc.).
  - type: kart-grid
    baslik: Symptoms of anxiety disorder
    giris: 'Symptoms can be grouped as emotional, cognitive and physical:'
    kolon: 3
    kartlar:
      - baslik: Emotional
        maddeler:
          - Persistent sense of dread
          - Irritability and tension
          - Fear of losing control
          - Panic and terror
      - baslik: Cognitive
        maddeler:
          - Difficulty concentrating
          - Catastrophic thinking
          - Indecisiveness
          - Mind going "blank"
      - baslik: Physical
        maddeler:
          - Palpitations, sweating
          - Muscle tension
          - Sleep problems
          - Shortness of breath
  - type: onayli-liste
    baslik: Treatment options
    giris: 'Anxiety disorders are largely manageable with appropriate treatment. The main evidence-based approaches are:'
    maddeler:
      - baslik: Cognitive Behavioural Therapy (CBT)
        aciklama: Focuses on recognising and changing the thought patterns that fuel anxiety. CBT has the strongest evidence base for anxiety disorders.
      - baslik: Trauma-Focused Therapy
        aciklama: Particularly effective for anxiety rooted in traumatic experiences.
      - baslik: Mindfulness-Based Approaches
        aciklama: Breaks the anxiety cycle by learning to stay present in the moment.
  - type: bilgi-kutusu
    ton: turuncu
    baslik: When should you seek help?
    metin: If your anxiety is negatively affecting your work, relationships or daily functioning; if you have developed avoidance behaviours; or if you are experiencing sleep difficulties, it is advisable to speak to a professional.
